  \title{Acceptance catalogue and open questions}
  \p{\ref{at-kr-0000} is the inventory; 1 is Δ comparison; 2 is the general nerve theorem with its hypotheses; 3 is explicit presentations; 4 is Θ_n; 5 is Δ's pattern; 6 is elegance for named adopted shapes; 7 is Ω's generalized-Reedy structure; 8 is the augmented discrete nerve theorem; 9 is labelled Δ; 10 is the exact Kan closure list; 11 is reduced Reedy replacement; 12/13/14 are deferred geometric comparisons. All are proposed until linked to Lean statements and proofs. \ref{ms-foundation} gates specify the subset needed early.}
  \p{\ref{oq-kr-0001}: choose the symmetric-operad arity proof when Ω is needed. \ref{oq-kr-0002}: establish an augmented arity presentation that handles empty outputs and vertical 2-cells; do not freeze the row encoding in advance. \ref{oq-kr-0003}: choose the Ω equivariant model separately from the root diagram model. \ref{oq-kr-0004}: if root elegance fails, identify an actual alternative with sufficient cofibrancy/replacement theorems, or revise the root model at \ref{ms-foundation}.}
